# The three seed homes, each of which must ship (MLB-114). `*.csv` above is
# a blanket ignore, so a seed directory that is not named here is invisible
# to git no matter what it contains -- a new template added later would be
# silently unshipped, and the demo fixture would not exist on a clone.
# These entries are what make "runnable by a stranger" survive.
!dbt_league/seeds/*.csv
!dbt_league/league_config/*.csv
!demo/league_config/*.csv
# The PII guard's disposition ledger (MLB-234), for the same reason: it is
# the DURABLE record of which review hits have been looked at, so a copy
# that only exists on one machine is not a record at all -- the next sweep
# would report every reviewed site as new. It carries no real-side value;
# each identity is an HMAC under a secret kept with the private map.
!tools/pii_dispositions.csv
output/leagueNoteHeader.txt
output/leagueNoteFooter.txt

