# MLB-154 root curation (2026-08-02): keep the root curated after the pass.
# Session exhaust lands in docs/ homes (see CLAUDE.md forward rule) or stays
# local -- it never becomes a tracked root file again.
#
# Every pattern here is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash, so the archive
# this pass just built (docs/archive/HANDOFF*.md) stays tracked. Without the
# anchors the rider would swallow the very files it was written to protect.
#
# All THREE handoff patterns are load-bearing; none is a duplicate:
#   /HANDOFF*.md   anchors to start-of-name  -- HANDOFF_OVERNIGHT_DOCS.md
#   /*HANDOFF*.md  catches a PREFIX          -- "PROJECT HANDOFF.md"
#   /*Handoff*.md  catches the other case    -- "GitHub Cleanup Handoff.md"
# gitignore matching is case-SENSITIVE, so the mixed-case pattern does not
# cover the shouted one and vice versa.
/HANDOFF*.md
/*HANDOFF*.md
/*Handoff*.md
/REVIEW.md
# The release PLAN is the maintainer's internal strategy doc (offline
# decisions, launch checklist, monetization thinking) -- deliberately local,
# NOT the tracked RELEASING.md ceremony. RELEASING.md used to point the
# announce step straight at it; that pointer now says it is untracked
# instead, so a fresh clone is not sent looking for a file it cannot have.
/RELEASE PLAN.md
/DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md
/DBT EXPLORATORY SWEEP.md
/v*.* Refactor Brief.md
# CLAUDE.md is the maintainer's working agreement with his Claude Code
# sessions -- house rules, standing corrections, the false alarms worth
# not re-raising. Internal-facing AND personal, which is what separates it
# from RELEASING.md: a release checklist is project process a stranger can
# read as discipline, this is a record of how one person works with a
# tool. Untracked at the 1.7.0 cut.
#
# The file STAYS ON DISK and keeps working: Claude Code reads it from the
# checkout, not from git, so nothing about the house rules changes.
#
# History is deliberately NOT rewritten. Measured rather than assumed: its
# history carries no sensitive strings, and the public timeline already
# has AI co-author trailers in other commits -- so a rewrite would hide
# nothing while force-pushing days before launch. Fix-forward stands.
/CLAUDE.md

